    "text_full": "Cookie Settings\nMain Content\nMain Menu\nSEARCH\nMENU\nPeople\nPractices\nInsights\nITC Finds Unfairly Traded Imports of Container Chassis and Subassemblies from Mexico, Thailand, and Vietnam Injure the U.S. Industry\nPRESS RELEASE\nMay 20, 2026\nOur Insights\n\nWith a deep understanding of Washington and a broad knowledge of legal and regulatory frameworks, Wiley is well-positioned to deliver sharp analysis on the most pressing issues. These are our insights on the challenges shaping the business and regulatory landscape today and beyond.\n\nWhat The \"New TSCA\" Has Accomplished - and What Comes Next\nThe American Bar Association's Section of Environment, Energy, and Resources\nARTICLE\nMay 19, 2026\nSeeds of Change: How Biotechnology is Reshaping Agriculture\nPODCAST\nMay 19, 2026\nTrending Topics\nArtificial Intelligence\nConsumer Protection\nCryptocurrency\nExecutive Orders\nFAR and DFARS Overhaul\nFederal Infrastructure\nFraud and Scams\nSCOTUS\nTariffs\nTrump Administration\nAPPEARANCES\nWiley in the Wild\n\nJoin us as we take the stage and share our legal expertise, providing valuable insights and engaging discussions on a wide range of topics.\n\nEVENT\nGRAS in Transition: Preparing for FDA’s New Rule and Its Impact on Supplement Compliance\nAmerican Conference Institute (ACI) and Council for Responsible Nutrition (CRN)\nAnn M. Begley\nJune 25, 2026\nEVENT\nTSCA Reform: Risk Management\nEnvironmental Law Institute\nMartha E. Marrapese\nJune 10, 2026\nWEBINAR\nCongressional Investigations: Oversight Powers and Practical Strategies for Navigating Risk\nJason McCullough, Diana R. Shaw, Brian Walsh\nMay 27, 2026\nPUBLICATION\nSeeds of Change: How Biotechnology is Reshaping Agriculture\nLauren Petrin, Alex L. D. Stanton, Ph.D.\nMay 19, 2026\nEVENT\nDigesting the Latest GRAS Reforms\nMichigan State University College of Law's Summer Conference\nAnn M. Begley, Lauren Petrin, Mary Beth Schultz\nMay 18, 2026\nMEDIA MENTION\nWiley Attorneys Noted by Law360 for Major First Amendment Ruling for Retail Energy Suppliers\nLaw360\nThomas M. Johnson, Jr., Stephen J. Obermeier, Jeremy J. Broggi, Krystal B. Swendsboe, Boyd Garriott, Joel S. Nolette\nMay 15, 2026\nMore Events\nMore Media Mentions\nMore Podcasts\nCATEGORIES:\nMedia Mentions\nPress Releases\nAlerts\nArticles\nBlogs\nNewsletters\nPodcasts & Videos\nEvents\nHandbooks\nWebinars\nLATEST FIRM NEWS\nITC Finds Unfairly Traded Imports of Container Chassis and Subassemblies from Mexico, Thailand, and Vietnam Injure the U.S. Industry\nMay 20, 2026\nWiley Receives Am Law Litigator of the Week Shout-Out for Historic Trade-Based FCA Recovery\nMay 15, 2026\nWiley Secures Major First Amendment Victory for Retail Energy Suppliers\nMay 15, 2026\nWiley Helps Secure Historic FCA Recovery in Aluminum Tariff Evasion Case\nMay 13, 2026\nLATEST PODCASTS & VIDEOS\nSeeds of Change: How Biotechnology is Reshaping Agriculture\nMay 19, 2026\nKeyboard Cartel: The Carbanak Story\nMay 14, 2026\nThe FCC’s Expanding Role in National Security\nMay 8, 2026\nEpisode 5: Defending Reality: Combating Synthetic Media Through Deepfake Response Coverage\nMay 7, 2026\nOUR PERSPECTIVES\nFrom Our Blogs\n\nWe dive into the intricacies of legal matters and provide insightful perspectives on the ever-evolving landscape of the legal world.\n\nWILEY CONNECT\nAI in Hiring: Evolving Legal Risks Under State and Federal Law\nMay 19, 2026\nRead More\nWILEY EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\nInterrelated Wrongful Act Provisions Do Not Create Coverage for Uncovered Claims\nMay 19, 2026\nRead More\nWILEY CONNECT\nThe FCC's Expanding Role in National Security\nMay 8, 2026\nRead More\nWILEY EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\nQui Tam Wage‑and‑Hour Action Not an “Employment Claim” and Thus No Duty to Defend\nMay 5, 2026\nRead More\nSign Up for Our Insights\n\nKeeping you updated on issues that may impact your business is our priority. With thought leaders in the legal and public policy sectors and the industries in which you operate, we continuously share our knowledge with you through published articles, client alerts and other timely materials. Please sign up to receive our Alerts and Publications.\n\nSubscribe\n\nFEATURED HANDBOOK\nThe Defense Counterintelligence and Security Agency (DCSA) and Foreign Ownership, Control or Influence (FOCI) Handbook\n\nWiley’s FOCI Handbook outlines the circumstances under which the DCSA grants security clearances that permit companies and their personnel to perform classified work. Items addressed in the handbook are FOCI mitigation instruments, the security review and rating process, and compliance, in addition to recent developments in FOCI enforcement.\n\nDownload the Handbook\n\nPeople\nPractices\nInsights\nFirm\nCareers\nInclusion and Engagement\nHome\nSite Map\nTerms & Conditions\nPrivacy Policy\nCookies Policy & Settings\nCalifornia Privacy Notice\n© 2026 Wiley Rein LLP All Rights Reserved.\nSubscribe\n\nOur Site uses cookies to improve your experience. Cookies may collect your personal information, such as IP address or device identifier, which we may disclose to our analytics partners. You may opt out of the cookies that are not strictly necessary if you wish. By using this site, you agree to our updated Privacy Policy, Terms & Conditions, and Cookies Policy.\n\nCUSTOMIZE COOKIE CHOICES\nREJECT ALL COOKIES\nACCEPT ALL COOKIES"
